# expect: break cannot apply to a parallel for (chunks cannot stop each other)
# A `parallel for` splits its range into chunks that run independently; one
# chunk cannot stop the others, so `break` has no meaning and is refused
# instead of breaking only its own chunk.
fn main():
    total := 0
    parallel for i in 0..<4:
        total = total + i
        break
    println(str(total))
